    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d647">

                <pb facs="0557" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg441"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/626.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Buckner to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 3, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s September 30. American missionary drafts discounted 8 per cent. Some
                    boarding schools closed for lack of food but no famine anywhere. Fifty-four
                    immigrants are destitute and appeal to me for aid.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buckner</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
